00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,760
So if you're closing four out of five people,

2
00:00:01,760 --> 00:00:04,280
80% or more, it means you're probably underpriced

3
00:00:04,280 --> 00:00:05,640
by three to four X.

4
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:07,640
If your close rate is 60 to 80%,

5
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:10,160
it probably means that you're underpriced by two to three X.

6
00:00:10,160 --> 00:00:12,120
If your close rate is 50 to 60%,

7
00:00:12,120 --> 00:00:14,000
it usually means you're underpriced by one to two X.

8
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,840
If your close rate is 40 to 50%,

9
00:00:15,840 --> 00:00:17,800
you're probably underpriced by one to one and a half.

10
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,160
And if your close rate is 30 to 40,

11
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:21,080
it means you're probably close to correctly priced.

12
00:00:21,080 --> 00:00:22,600
Now if your close rate is below 30 or less,

13
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:23,840
it means you probably have an avatar

14
00:00:23,840 --> 00:00:26,080
or sales process problem rather than pricing,

15
00:00:26,080 --> 00:00:26,960
so fix that first.

16
00:00:26,960 --> 00:00:28,480
And to be clear, these are just rules of thumbs

17
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:30,760
